#!/bin/bash
# omarchy-wsl-help - the cheat sheet shown after install.

cat <<'EOF'

  omarchy-wsl2 - Omarchy on WSL2

  MODE 1  Headless (terminal only)
    wsl -d omarchy                 open a shell from Windows
    fastfetch                      system summary
    lazygit / btop / nvim          the Omarchy TUI staples

  MODE 2  Individual GUI apps via WSLg
    omarchy-wsl-app chromium       run one app as a Windows window
    omarchy-wsl-app foot           Omarchy's terminal
    (GUI apps also work directly once you have logged in interactively)

  MODE 3  Full desktop (sway - Hyprland cannot run under WSL2)
    omarchy-wsl-desktop            nested inside WSLg (one window)
    omarchy-wsl-desktop --size 1600x900   set that window's size
                                   (it has no titlebar: Alt+Space or Win+Up
                                    are Windows' own move/maximise controls)
    omarchy-wsl-desktop vnc        full screen over VNC on 127.0.0.1:5900
    omarchy-wsl-desktop vnc --size 2560x1440 --port 5901
    omarchy-wsl-desktop --floating draggable windows with titlebars
    omarchy-wsl-desktop --tiling   back to Omarchy's tiling model

    VNC full screen is the RECOMMENDED mode: SUPER keys work (WSLg steals
    them when nested) and it composites once instead of twice.
      Windows:  winget install -e --id TigerVNC.TigerVNC
      Connect:  127.0.0.1:5900     Leave full screen: F8 (Ctrl+M on 1.16+)
    Clipboard works both ways in both modes; VNC is text-only.

  KEYS IN THE DESKTOP   (SUPER = the Windows key)
    New to tiling? These five are enough to get started:
      SUPER+Return      open a terminal
      SUPER+W           close the focused window
      SUPER+Space       launcher
      SUPER+H / L       move focus left / right
      SUPER+F           fullscreen

    Then:
      SUPER+J / K            focus down / up (arrows work too)
      SUPER+Shift+H/J/K/L    move the window itself
      SUPER+1..9             switch workspace
      SUPER+Shift+1..9       move window to workspace
      SUPER+V / G            split vertical / horizontal
      SUPER+T                tabbed layout
      SUPER+Shift+Space      toggle floating for this window
      SUPER+R                resize mode (arrows/hjkl, Esc to finish)
      SUPER + left-drag      move a floating window
      SUPER + right-drag     resize any window
      SUPER+B / E            browser / file manager
      Print / Shift+Print    region screenshot / full screen to clipboard
      SUPER+Shift+R          reload config
      SUPER+Shift+E          exit the session

    Note: nested in WSLg, Windows claims some SUPER combos first.
          VNC mode does not have this problem.

  THEMING
    omarchy-theme-set "Tokyo Night"      switch theme
    omarchy-theme-list                   what is available
    omarchy-wsl-bg                       list backgrounds (* = current)
    omarchy-wsl-bg 3 | next              set the 3rd, or cycle
    omarchy-wsl-bg ~/pic.png             use your own image
    ~/.config/omarchy/                   your overrides

  PACKAGES
    sudo pacman -Syu <pkg>         install (always -Syu, never bare -Sy)
    omarchy-pkg-add <pkg>          Omarchy's wrapper for the same
    pacman -Q                      list what's installed

  CREDENTIALS
    omarchy-wsl-keyring            fix "System keychain unavailable" prompts
    omarchy-wsl-keyring --status   what's running

  DIAGNOSTICS
    omarchy-wsl-doctor             check WSLg / GPU / systemd / desktop

  APPEARANCE
    omarchy-wsl-wt -i              style the Windows Terminal profile
    omarchy-wsl-wt --restore       undo the last Terminal change

  LEARN
    oml "how do I change theme"    ask the built-in Omarchy/WSL2 tutor
    omarchy-learn --check          verify Copilot CLI + auth
    omarchy-learn --topics         suggested starter questions

  DEV TOOLS
    sudo omarchy-wsl-devtools gh mise docker
    sudo omarchy-wsl-devtools --list

  WINDOWS INTEROP
    explorer.exe .                 open the current dir in File Explorer
    code .                         open VS Code (WSL remote)
    wsl.exe --shutdown             (from Windows) restart the VM

  Docs: /usr/share/omarchy-wsl2/docs  (start with 13-post-install.md)
        Why sway and not Hyprland: 12-wayland-on-wsl2.md
        Upstream manual: https://omarchy.org/manual/

EOF
